A||||45||My7Fieros||COME ON GUYS!!!!!||||8||
Z||000000||My7Fieros||01-10-2001||07:35 PM||||Ok listen, I really try to avoid b1tch sessions, but this has been really bugging me. Whenever I have a problem w/ my Fiero, mechanical that is, I post it in the TD&Q section. <I>Usually</I> its something that needs quick attention (car wont start, running bad, ect.)and this forum is the perfect place to get (usually fast) advice. <BR>But the thing that bugs me is when I post a legit problem, and come back later only to find it bumped down to the bottom of the list with little to no response, while topics such as speaker placement, V8s, nitrous, badges, ect get top priority and the most replies. If theres a problem with my car, I would hope to get some replies, as Im sure you would to..I try to help whenever I can...thats why we're here. I dont mind talking about the speakers and "how to get my Fiero to do 1/4 miles in such and such time", but lets read the topics and try to be helpful to those of us who need help with our getting our cars running..ok? <BR>Like I said, I hate to belly ache, but sometimes it gets kind of discouraging. All in all this forum is the greatest, but......you know? Thanx for letting me vent.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://tgowens.com/My7Fieros_sig.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 01-10-2001).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||RaeQwan||01-10-2001||07:40 PM||||We'll excuse you're belly aching this time.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> we all do it sometimes<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/raeqwansig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Philphine||01-10-2001||07:50 PM||||i usually can't answer the tech questions. if it's an interesting question i check back to see the answer myself. better not to get one than an uneducated one. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||01-10-2001||08:03 PM||||i try to only post on questions i have direct knowlege of. If i dont know i go to the next topic .||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cheever2||01-10-2001||08:14 PM||||My7, there are just so many problems to post.  As much as I hate those forums who have a zillion categories, maybe our cosmetic Tech questions should be separated from drivetrain/mechanical questions.  Just saying it without really thinking it over.<P>I also wonder if engine swaps should have their own section, since there are so many topics at any given time regarding those.<P>Don't want to start any controversy.  Just trying to help.<P><P>------------------<BR><I>Chuck Hodges</I>||||reg||6
Z||000005||Old Lar||01-10-2001||08:25 PM||||I'm in the same boat as Philphine, I'm at a loss as to some of the solution to some of the more complex problems.  Most of the speaker fixes, NOS and V8 upgrades are people experimenting with these modifications and searches for opinions as to the changes.<P>After over a year of help suggestions I see help:  Fuses, carbon buildup in intake manifold, ER tube/EGR valve/EGR selinoid, fuel filter, MAP Sensor, IAC sensor, O2 sensor, ignition module, tach filter, spark plugs/wires, battery, computer, alternator, clogged catalytic converter. Error codes?<P>Breaks down to no juice, no fuel, vaccuum leak.  Review the trouble shooting guide in the Haynes Manual and hope something pops out.  Hard to diagnose problems over a computer script.<P>I can't diagnose whats wrong with my car (code 32). I go to a more knowledgable mechanic.  Mr Goodwrench and his $can tools. The only advise I have is that it is usually th simplist things go wrong and they are so easily overlooked.<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000006||MrPBody||01-10-2001||08:27 PM||||It's lots harder to diagnose a broken car than to express an opinion on speakers.<P>Call that the "usefulness-to-abundance ratio"?<BR>||||reg||12
Z||000007||Coconut||01-10-2001||09:29 PM||||My7, I do think you have a legitimate ***** . I've been fortunate with having my problems commented on, so I really can't complain, however....in light of the tremendous growth that PFF is experiencing, it's unfortunate that you've been having to deal with your posts seemingly overlooked. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  I do believe that every Forum member here is glad to help where they feel they have the expertise to post accordingly. Philiphine is correct though, better to get no answer than an uneducated one. Perhaps Cliff could consider the suggestion that Cheever2 mentioned. I for one think it may be a great idea to have a seperate category for cosmetic or stereo type postings in addition to a stricly mechanically related only posting area. Of course, I really don't know how much work that would entail for our gracious moderator! I haven't the foggiest idea as to the practicality of being able to add a new category! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> What say you, Cliff?<P>Cruisin' <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Coconut's_Signature_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroLisa||01-10-2001||09:40 PM||||A lot of us are just as inexperienced about your problem as you are  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I agree no answer is better than an uneducated one. <BR>As for the other questions, well I don't always have problems with my car, but just like you don't know why there is some knocking sound, I might not know how to wire up a stereo amp I want. They are all important questions, regardless of what they are about. <BR>And I also think that most people (including me! ) have more opinions than knowledge sometimes  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> So the opinion posts are easier to reply to. <P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (Sold!)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<BR>*As Always, Updated Website*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000009||My7Fieros||01-10-2001||10:22 PM||||Good points everyone...Id have to agree that "no reply is better than an uneducated one" I guess. I hate to gripe, but I guess owning one (or several in my case) of these cars can get to be a headache sometimes!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>I have kinda been wondering about adding more catagories to the forum. Ive looked into several other forums (like the MR2 and the LS1 or whatever the Firebird/Camaro one is) and noticed that they have many many different catagories. I wonder if Cliff wouldnt consider doing something like that...perhaps a "Technical/Mechanical, need engine help now" kinda thing...or an "Exterior mod/Interior mod" kinda thing....hmmmmmmm.<BR>Sometimes I (as well as most everyone else) need help and seeing a reply that "hits the nail right on the head" really makes your day..ya know? I try to make it a point to read most all the TD&Q's, even the ones that dont sound to "juicy"....everyone posts a topic for a reason (usually lol).<BR>Anyway, sorry to gripe.......   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://tgowens.com/My7Fieros_sig.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 01-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||jerpro||01-10-2001||10:40 PM||||I know where you are coming from. <BR>I have posted questions that have gone completely unanswered and yes, it is frustrating. <BR>And I had to go do research on other fiero sites and in one instance I had to go ask a mechanic.<BR>It is all the roll of the dice.<BR>What I do know is that there are several mechanics on this forum, but it simply looks like they overlook those questions.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Philphine||01-10-2001||10:42 PM||||if you want to see a forum with a lot of categories, look for the corvette forum (format just like this one). i don't think we need anything near that complex, but maybe an idea or two can be tried here, cliff willing (hmmm...i'm not sure if that sounded right). or if a number of people think there's a good idea from there.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Indiana_resto_guy||01-10-2001||11:08 PM||||MY7,<P>Lots of times, it is impossible to give direct answers to some problems for several reasons.<BR>Inadequate conditions, too brief descriptions of the problems (ie: car won't start?)<BR>Even mechanics can't say for sure what the problem may be without looking or hearing for themselves!<BR>I'm not saying that this is you in any way, shape or form. With 7 in your yard you should have a good bit of knowledge with several problems. It may help if you recieve no replys to say what it isn't to help narrow down some of the issues that may be involved. I have tooooo many hanging here my self and have 3 more on the way. Lots of times the same problem can have different causes, don't get discoruaged just bump it back up and add to if necessary by replying to your own thread, it makes people look more anyway.<BR>Hang in there!||||reg||1
Z||000013||DaRkLoRD||01-10-2001||11:24 PM||||I think tech section sub-categories would be great.. a section for mods, one for engine/transmission repair, engine swaps, etc..<P>you've got my vote for this.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||14
Z||000014||Terrybogin||01-10-2001||11:35 PM||||Come on now, Cliff does this for us with no financial help whatsoever. Let's NOT start looking a gift horse in the mouth! ||||reg||1
Z||000015||fropuff||01-10-2001||11:55 PM||||I'm sure everyone hates it when they're in a hurry.  I've been there a few times.  I also use the e-mail notifier, and it also makes me a little upset when someone says something that it totally off-topic.  The only good thing I see with that is that they bump the post to the top.  Oh well.  Sorry about the nitrous questions.  They're usually me.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000016||2xsess||01-11-2001||12:00 AM||||I've had the same problem My7. I've had serious tech problems go unanswered, it's dissapointing but I've also come to realize that it's hard to trouble shoot a car via internet. I read almost all of the tech posts and try to answer the ones I've had experience with. A lot of times I find myself checking back to learn the answer myself.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||DXR_DAD||01-11-2001||12:51 AM||||I don't like to get into these type posts, but here goes. I think everyone has made good points!!!. I have found that if you keep your post at the top it will get a reply maybe not as fast as you need it but it will come  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. jerpro, you make a good point: <BR>(Quote)<BR><B>What I do know is that there are several mechanics on this forum, but it simply looks like they overlook those questions.</B><P>We do have some "Fiero Mechanics" here and some that are "FIERO SELLER" or in a "FIERO BUSINESS" those were the people we look to for answers??<P>Here's somthing that may also help. When someone ask a price for a part or who has it, could that person just post the answer, and not say call me. As stated here others are looking for the same part, this will keep them from having to post the same question again.<BR>This also applys to the tech section, if you have the answer just post it so others will have that info or new members will be able to do a search and get it. The "call me" thing is not helping everyone, remember somebody is going to have the same problem next week?? I have done many repairs on my fiero just remembering an old post  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> That has been a big help to me and I'm sure it will help others. With all the new member we get the same ?'s over and over.<P>Well that's my 0.02<P>THANKS<BR>DXR_DAD<P>PS. PFF still the best spot on the net!<P> ||||reg||1
Z||000018||tgowens||01-11-2001||01:16 AM||||ok My7, I respond to posts if I know the answer -- I am still learning myself (and I work on these things all day every day) - guess you could call me a "mechanic in training"<P>And Dad - one of the reasons I ask that people call is because more than once someone has inquired about an "automatic selector cable" when what they really needed was an automatic throttle valve cable", or maybe it's because they have asked about a "gray trim fascia" and I know that there are three colors of gray (or silver) trim fascias........sometimes it is just easier to get it worked out via phone rather than in posts on the forum and the same goes with mechanical - in fact, especially with mechanical -- like it was said earlier, sometimes a description of a sysmptom on the forum is not enough to elicit the proper diagnosis. And.........if they want to call they will call and if not they won't........I am here to help, the Fiero Shop is here to help - in any way we can......we give free advice everyday - no charge!<P>My7, it IS understandable and I think it has happened to us all. I remember when I first got my Fiero I didn't know squat about it (some say I still don't) but now, after months of working here at the shop I have learned much more. But, like all of us (owners) we know enough to get by sometimes -- there are things I feel confident about doing on these cars and those are the posts I am likely to answer. If I don't feel that I am qualified to answer I generally don't. Everyone on here has a different expertise on these cars due to their involvement with them........but - that's why we are all here - to share knowledge and to learn from it.........and........if you can't find the answer here, call me - I'll find out (sorry Bill, I just couldn't resist!)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000019||007DOUG||01-11-2001||01:23 AM||||I first do a search of old tech topics.<BR> <BR>Then I visit the cave.<P>Then I post a question when I've exhausted the above.<P>I've noticed alot of posted questions that have been answer many times over in the past. AND THATS OK. But whomever posted the question might be able to get an instant answer by doing a search. <P>My only gripe is when you post a problem, explain it clearly in the topic. That way, when someone does a topic search in the future, the question (and answers) will be easy to find. <P>Its hard to search through old tech topics when when your topic header reads "I give-up", or "Now what?". I have no idea what those threads are about.<P>------------------<BR>5 Indy pace Cars<BR>84 T-top<BR>84 SE<BR>86 SE V6 153K<BR>86 GT<BR>86 GT now with a 4:10<BR>86 GT 3.4 Pearl White T-top<BR>2 88 GT's (twins)<P>However......<BR><I>"Time is my most precious and most perishable of all my possessions."</I>||||reg||6
Z||000020||DXR_DAD||01-11-2001||01:46 AM||||Terry, I was just saying that to help the next person, so that he/she doesn't make the same mistake &lt; Throttle valve cable/Selector cable&gt;. If the info was here they would not have to ask the same question?? When I posted the ? about the trim fascia you quickly replyed with an answer, <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> now anyone can do a search and find that info.<P>I'm with Doug, I just did a search the other day just to find some info on painting and prep work (that may be a hint)??<BR>there was a ton of info<P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||14
Z||000021||Archie||01-11-2001||01:57 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>i try to only post on questions i have direct knowlege of. If i dont know i go to the next topic .</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I agree with Roger. I'll answer what I know for fact, but the only thing I know for sure about stock Fieros is how to take them apart.<P>I've NEVER had to put a stock Fiero together or make it run. I've never even changed spark plugs on a stock Fiero.<P>The good thing is that I've never been broke down or stranded by a non-stock Fiero.<P>What did people do for answers before the Internet?, Man, can you imagine what it was like BI (Before Internet)?<P>Just think of those old pioneers who had to work on thier Fieros without the aid of the internet.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Archie<p>[This message has been edited by Archie (edited 01-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||mrfixit58||01-11-2001||09:34 AM||||Don't forget this site:<P>"The On-line Service Guide" <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/osg.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/osg.html</A> <P>I've found it very helpful with small repairs.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000023||william_thorniii||01-11-2001||09:52 AM||||My 7,<P>First of all... yes we are all conciesly making an effort to neglect your tech questions.  Perhaps we excluded you from all of the previous PFF against My 7 Fieros meetings.  Second of all, I ONLY open threads that specifically relate to a problem in the title.  I find it a waste of my time to try to read every thread.  If it is titled "Hey Guys, Look at This"... I will never open it.  It is a two way street.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||13
Z||000024||BN Boomer||01-11-2001||10:25 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 007DOUG:<BR><B><BR>I first do a search of old tech topics.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ding, ding, ding, ding, ding, ding!<P>We have a winner! I'm surprised it took so long for someone to mention it.<P>If you haven't already tried searching, I don't think you really have a legitimate gripe.<P>You should really try the search function first. Many times, topics have already been discussed at length numerous times. I honestly believe that some of the regulars and more knowledgable among us occassionally just get plain tired of answering the same questions over and over.<P>I can't think of a single problem that I have had with my own Fieros where I couldn't find a wealth of information just by using the search function. When searching, try different words and phrases to describe what you are looking for. Chances are that you will come up with enough material related to your problem to keep you reading for quite some time as well as help to cure whatever ails your Fiero. <P>Anyhow, that's my 2 cents, and we all know just how far that will get you these days.||||reg||1
Z||000025||terryk||01-11-2001||12:03 PM||||I think everyone here tries to help when they can, but as the problem becomes more and more technical, the number of people that can answer becomes less and less. There are many things I just can't answer (I know little about, i.e. suspensions/yes, I hate poly...) or I'm afraid of getting into a contest with someone (200lb injectors on a Duke).<P>I know one problem I have is that I get asked questions in the middle of a thread. I just happen to notice my name while buzzing the "Four Wings Stacked Up on the Rear Deck = Ricer?" thread asking me about some ECM item. I feel like I ignored them. <P>We just about need a volunteer list of people that are willing to help on problems in different categories (with no obligation). A person could put their name on the list and what things they are willing to discuss without *any* obligation or responsibility (now that's having it both ways). There will always be people that take and don't return, but that's life. It all depends on how much we want out of this. I've learned tons from this place.<P>Finally, if you know certain people might have the information or solution you need, email them directly. It's amazing how much more talkative people are in direct conversations!<P>IMHO....||||reg||1
Z||000026||Cliff Pennock||01-11-2001||02:33 PM||||M7F, you bring up a good point. And it's a problem I have been thinking about for a long time now. I know the Search option can answer a lot of problems but it is always hard to find the information you want.<P>I've come to the conclusion that I <B>do</B> want to split up the TD&Q section, but I don't want a zillion sections like most other forums. The problem with many sections is that a lot of people will never visit some sections because the section's title alone is something they (think they) know nothing about.<P>This is what I am willing to do: split up the TD&Q section in three (or four at the most). Or in other words: add two (or three) more sections. For example:<P><UL TYPE=SQUARE><LI>Mechanical<BR><LI>Electrical<BR><LI>Engine swaps<BR><LI>Miscellaneous<BR></UL><P>Like I said, this is just an example so I'm open for suggestions. But please, no more than 4 sections (and I want to keep the Miscellaneous section to store the current TD&Q section in).<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000027||tgowens||01-11-2001||02:49 PM||||great idea Cliff, the only problem I can see tho is that (and we all know this) on the Fiero an electrical malfunction can create a mechanical problem and a mechanical problem can create an electrical malfunction - now, which category do I post my question in?<P>I might suggest these categories:<P><B>General</B> (anything not covered in other categories <I>or</I> if not not clear which category to post in)<BR><B>Mechanical</B> (purely mechanical, if known)<BR><B>Electrical</B> (purely electrical, if known)<BR><B>Performance Upgrades</B> (engine swaps, suspension upgrades, brake upgrades, etc)<BR><B>Modifications</B> (this would be interior and exterior mods, i.e. scoops, wheels, stereo systems, etc......)<P>I realize that is five categories but that should just about cover anything we may need to post in the TD&Q section........<P>just my 3 cents (had to raise my rates!)<P>Also, is there any way that those of us connected with a shop or working as a vendor could post an icon which would take someone to the name, address and phone number of that source? A lot of the Fiero world has to search the internet constantly to find a source for parts and services when sometimes the source is very close to them but they are just not aware of it........in other words, if we at the Fiero Shop had a specific icon which could be posted as a part of a signature, I could post a message with that icon and by clicking on it the original poster would be taken to the name and address of the shop. I realize that we can create a hyperlink in the signature so maybe this will have to suffice.<P>Also a thought, a "links" section where owners and business could post info about their web site or business?<P><BR>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 01-11-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 01-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000028||Oreif||01-11-2001||03:07 PM||||I think breaking up the Tech session would be great. The 4 catagories Cliff came up with sound very good. Also, what about members who are "in the business" writing articles and submitting them to ogre for the cave? I know we have members that paint Fiero's Maybe one of them could write up a quick article on what to do to paint a car. or Archie could write something about V-8 installs. I'm not talking an in depth 50 page report, But something that gives a basic outline so others can get an idea whats involved. I have noticed as an example that many are asking about refinishing the stock wheels. I'm sure a small article about each wheel would aid others and possible cut down duplicate threads.<P>One other helpful hint, Cliff, Could it be possible to add a message in the main tech area (or the title page) about ogre's cave and what it contains? When I first joined, I followed a link to the forum title page and I never even noticed that ogre had a cave let alone what the cave was all about. I am seeing a lot of new screen names and was thinking they may not know what the cave is either. (Of course after finding out what the cave was, I was able to find lots of helpful info.)<BR>Just my thoughts for today.<BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000029||80's BOY||01-11-2001||05:52 PM||||hey guys, i just read the thread. it sounds great, Cliff and thanks for all you've done so far. i could have never finished my 85 GT's engine or Targa without all the help/opinions from this forum. i would like to suggest simpler categories, though. such as:<BR>      --exterior--<BR>      --interior--<BR>      --performance mods--<BR>      --engine and tranny--<P>in my opinion, engine swaps fall under the "performance mods" category and people will always put their opinions and visit whichever category appeals or interests tham the most. everyone here is full of good ideas, just thought i'd add mine.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR> ||||reg||14
Z||000030||Cheever2||01-11-2001||09:56 PM||||My $.02 suggestion would be in direct response to my7fieros' predicament.  That is to have categories that reflect the seriousness of the problem.<BR>1)-Car can't be driven, need help asap<BR>2)-Runs but has problems<BR>3)-Engine swaps & other mechanical what-if's<BR>4)-Cosmetics & fluff mod's<P>But I'll go with whatever Cliff decides.  You done mighty good to get this where it is, man.<BR> ||||reg||6
Z||000031||tgowens||01-11-2001||10:57 PM||||fluff mods? Chuck, you have "fluff" mods on your car? Is that like fuzzy dice hanging from the mirror and that fuzzy thing around the mirror??.............(by the way, your tickets are on the way to you - we got just a little behind!)||||reg||1
Z||000032||Black88GT||01-11-2001||11:02 PM||||Thats a good idea Cliff.  I agree with you about those zillion topic forums.  Its so confusing and you can almost never visit them all and search through them.  However I guess they are needed for forums that offer such a wide variety of things to so many people.  For example, the Honda-Tech forum (www.hondaforum.com), that import scene is huge and "Honda" name sums up A LOT of cars and people.  For the Fiero forum, they are not needed though.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
Z||000033||ray b||01-12-2001||01:18 AM|||| cliff thans for all your work.if poster would put more info in title may help to quicken responce time. good addition would be links lists with rateings or comments. lastly edited hints made of best of forum posts,  real time eater but could farm out to members to do. I sure many would like to help.    ray<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000034||2xsess||01-12-2001||02:50 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 80's BOY:<BR><B><BR>      --exterior--<BR>      --interior--<BR>      --performance mods--<BR>      --engine and tranny--<BR> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I like this idea. The only thing would be where to put suspension and brake problems.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000035||theogre||01-12-2001||08:10 PM||||Alert! Very long post. Some ranting included. (Be Alert, The World Needs More Lerts.)<P>To start with, this isn't the first time this sort of thing has come up. Frankly, it peeves me considerably. <P>1. This IS NOT a live support forum. If you have an emergency, this is the wrong place for you. People providing information here do it because they feel like it and when time permits. There is no paid support staff here.<P>2. There are 1800+ members and counting. There are maybe 20-30 members actually qualified to answer the majority of questions. There are a more that can answer questions only on specific topics. Many of the 1800+ registered users are post and ghost. They post one or two items, get their answer and are rarely seen afterwards.<P>3. This IS NOT a live support forum. People are not sitting here waiting to help you. If you haven't gotten an answer, either no one knows or the ones that know haven't been here yet. The resent increase in volume does mean some questions may be missed. <B>This is not intentional.</B><P>4. I don't believe breaking up the forums will solve the original problem. It could actually make the problems worse. People are regularly posting things in the wrong place even with the small number of forums we have. More Forums may mean more work for people responding to problems and threads split all over creation. This has to be done very, very, carefully.<P>5. This IS NOT a live support forum. Qualified people will try to answer you when they are here. Depending on the topic and when it is posted, there may be 24 hours or more of delay in getting a useful response. <P>6. As someone pointed out above. We are seeing many of the same questions repeatedly. My "form answer" of using search and/or reading a particular cave article will likely become a very common response to many posts. I'm not going to keep typing the same answers again and again. I'll be happy to help if there are still questions after using search, etc.<P>7. This IS NOT a live support forum. Have I gotten this point across yet? If you get an answer the same day be happy. If you get one in a few hours consider yourself lucky.<P>8. If anything, we've reached the point where published Terms of Service and a guide page are needed. New users should have to click thru the TOS before anything else in the registration process. TOS doesn't have to be huge but needs more detail than forum.htm<P>9. We could have links to various commercial sites easy enough. They are usually banner ads these days. We don't want to get too many links on the forum pages. Those pages are pretty cluttered as it is. Adding more to them loads up the server and makes them take longer to load in your browser. (Cliff just upgraded the server. I think he'd like it to last awhile.) Keep in mind each page you see in the forum is dynamically created. That presents quit a load on the server compared to static pages like my cave. ((I also think that persistent commercial links should be paid for. But that's a whole other topic…))<P>10. We need to make some existing items more obvious. The search button for one. Search should be a big clear item on the main index and the topic pages.<P>11. The forums have multiple entry points. The forum entry needs to pass thru a single page like <A HREF="http://www.pennock.nl/forum.htm" TARGET=_blank>www.pennock.nl/forum.htm</A>  so that we can have a MOTD that reminds people to use things like Search before posting. (A link to the TOS should also appear clearly on this page.) Info like scheduled down time would also appear here.<P>12. We need a short guide to the search function to make it more accessible to new users. This guide should include key words to common items like clutches and brakes. This guide should also point out the archives. I think many people don't know they are there or have forgotten them.<P>Cliff spends at least a couple hours a day on site maintenance. The site also costs thousands of dollars a year for him to operate. He provides all of this FREE to the public.<P>I spend 1-2 hours a day during the week here, maybe more on the weekend. I don't get paid to be here. I like to help but I have other things to do. I simply don't have time to cover the volume of posts that are coming in. (This long post was written offline.)<P>I work in the forums in addition to the considerable time I spend on working in the Fiero Cave. I have projects like the current tech threads about the Blazer/Grand Am brake upgrade to work on. That one topic has more than 20 hours of research into it this week alone.<P>2xsess made the comment it is hard to diagnose over the Internet. It's even harder when people don't even check commonsense items or tell you what kind of car/setup it is. I lost count long ago of how many times the next message is "What motor and year?"  Then you find out they haven't even done the simple crap like check the battery connections. <P>I agree with some of the other posts above. I normally don't read threads like this one. I read this one because I was asked to.  If the tittle looks like someone is just showing car pic's or complaining about something I don't even open it. I only have so much time to read threads and respond.<P>Terryk has one of the best points. Digression of threads in tech is a giant pain in the rear. All of us have been guilty of that at one time or another but with the current volume of posts everyone has to avoid this. It's better to open a new thread and put in a reference to a related thread. For example, if we are talking about a problem in the ECM don't ask us about programming it. Start a new thread and if need be put in a link to the other one if it is somehow related to your programming question.<P>I really don't think breaking up the tech forum will help much with volume related problems. It may help with organization but it doesn't solve the lack of qualified people to answer questions. We'll still have about the same issues in responding.<P>If we do go that route we have to be very thorough in how we do it. The new tittles need to be very clear. After looking at the proposals above I came up with these…<P>Leave General to collect whatever. <BR>Move the old tech forum to archives. <BR>Body & Interior<BR>Powertrain (Engine & Transmission Systems)<BR>Chassis (Suspension & Brake Systems)<BR>Electrical System<BR>Heating Cooling and Air Conditioning (maybe.)<P>I don't see a need to split performance out to another category if we pick the main ones carefully. Most performance issues relate directly to one of the four-five I've broken them out to above.<P>A users guide for Search becomes even more important once we change the topic layout. We want to do something on the search page itself to push people to search the archived threads in addition to the new areas.<P>Tgowans, You can put UBB code in your sig tag. That will allow you to get a nicer looking link. I don't think it will allow a linked icon. The format for a link is {url=http://whatever.com}your text here{/url} Use square brackets in place of the curly ones.<P>Orief, We have areas on the <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl</A>  main index for the kind of articles you've proposed. I don't know what Cliff's rules might be for putting things in it are. I'm running out of space in my site. The time will come where I either have to stop adding new items or pay for more space. Most of the people "in the business" already have web sites where such articles can go. I don't keep a separate links page but if you've read some of my more recent cave articles, you'll see many links to other related sites/articles. Older articles have been gaining such links as I rework them for various reasons.<BR><P>------------------<BR><I><B>Screamin Yellow Zonkers... If it's Screamin and Yellow, I ain't eatin it.</B></I>||||reg||1
