Z||000040||Greg Piet||01-13-2001||05:29 AM||||Cliff mentioned the search function.<BR>I dont know how many threads there are on things like burping the radiatior, or bleeding the clutch, or headlight motor repair but its A LOT!<BR>To be honest I do NOT reply to posts where the info has been covered in more than 2 threads, unless the new thread says I looked but couldnt find the answer.<P>some one else said this but I will say it as well. USE THE FIERO ONLINE SERVICE GUIDE!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000041||theogre||01-13-2001||11:19 AM||||My7, If you took what I said above as a personal attack, you need to read it again. It comments on most of the preceeding messages in the thread and includes items In addition to the ideas posted above.<P>We have a major problem developing on this system. A problem of enough scope to kill the whole site if it is let go. You are not the only person that has complained that you didn't get an answer quickly. You likely aren't the only person to have a message missed lately.<P>The problem cause is 2 fold. The shear volume of posts are exceeding the ability of the few people that can answer them. A growing number of people comming here don't understand how the place works.<P>Like it or not, Fiero has become a niche car. There are very few people who have the background in these cars to fully support them. Even I don't cover everything. (I've spent hundreds of hours at least collecting the data for cave articles.)<P>Someone above made the comment that there are a number of mechanics here. I doubt there are more than a couple besides myself. The simple fact is most "profesional" mechanics won't touch a fiero unless they have to. Even when they do it's 50/50 at best that you won't end up more screwed up than when they started.<P>We have few general people. We have some others, like Archie and TerryK that are specialized in most of whet they do. We have other people who can cover the regular maintenance kind of stuff. There are going to be holes in coverage. Both in time and who knows what.||||reg||1
Z||000042||fropuff||01-13-2001||12:17 PM||||I know that some of you would rather type in a subject, look for some previous posts, and by the time you're done looking, someone has answered.  I've done this myself when I really want to know something.  There are tons of places that you can look for help.  I'll give you some: <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html</A>  <A HREF="http://www.carlynx.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.carlynx.com</A>   You'll have to click on the Pontiac and search for Fiero sites; there's plenty of them there. <A HREF="http://www.cvalley.net/~tevans/fiero/Skwyrul.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cvalley.net/~tevans/fiero/Skwyrul.htm</A>   This is the best one I've found by far.  I printed it out and it's 83 pages worth of information!!  Great place to look!<BR>Okay, so there's a few places that I also look, as well as Pennock's search function.  As far as not getting answered quickly, which is very frustrating, I don't know much about Fieros at all.  I'm just a kid, so I would rather not say anything than say something that I think is a guess.  I will just have to learn to live with this not being a public forum.   <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000043||My7Fieros||01-13-2001||02:15 PM||||Ok. Listen, I guess I took Ogre's post as a personal attack. If it wasnt, then I apologize. My point to the post was not about speedy answers..it was simply about "serious" questions getting no attention while the "fluff" questions got all the responses. Its no biggie, it was just something that bugged me from time to time, and I wanted to bring it up.<BR>I spend alot of time on here (prob too much lol), but when owning these cars, you really have to. Ive been on other Fiero "forum" type things in which the people were so incredibly rude and unresponsive, I ditched it (Im sure most of you know what Im talking about).<BR>Anyway I dont have any negative feelings towards anyone on here. If it werent for Ogre and others, none of my cars would be running right now...that much I know! Anyway lets just color this done...k? Thanx again.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://tgowens.com/My7Fieros_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000044||Sage||01-13-2001||05:19 PM||||Good show chaps.<BR>What I mean is, it's good to see people get things worked out through communication.<P>"Communication is the key to understanding;<BR>understanding is the key to happiness."<P>Corny?  Maybe...but I like it!<P>Have a good one!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000045||tgowens||01-14-2001||01:22 AM||||theogre said: <P><B>Like it or not, Fiero has become a niche car. There are very few people who have the background in these cars to fully support them. Even I don't cover everything....</B><P>This is true, it is a niche car. We are constantly learning about them and I work on them all day every day and I am still amazed and fascinated at what I learn daily.<P><B>Someone above made the comment that there are a number of mechanics here. I doubt there are more than a couple besides myself....</B><P>Now, I take exception to <I>this</I> statement - there are <B>many</B> people here who are qualified to answer questions based on their mechanical abilities. I, for one, work in a specialized shop dedicated to the repair and restoration of the Pontiac Fiero (Fiero Shop)- that's all we work on - take a look at Fiero Factory, Twin Lakes Fiero, etc - there are quite a few in this country specialized - at least far more than just a "couple" besides theogre. While I respect his knowledge and expertise, I think the statement was somewhat misleading to the new members of the forum who do not know us.<P><B>We have few general people. We have some others, like Archie and TerryK that are specialized in most of whet they do.</B><P>Once again, a statement indicating that these indivuduals are to be the "authority" (I do realize that the word "like" was used) -- as I said - there are several -- Again, I respect Archie and TerryK for their knowledge and expertise with the V-8 in the Fiero (even Archie mentioned that he does very little work on a <I>stock</I> Fiero) -- <P>We are here to learn, to share knowledge, and to teach - that's what this forum is all about. But, let's not give the younger (I'm 53 so there are a LOT of members here younger than me!) members the impression that there are only certain ones here to be trusted with answering technical questions.<P>And, once again, I applaud Cliff for making the forum possible and for allowing us to "vent" at times as well as helping someone replace their clutch! - And, Cliff.....as a webmaster (<I>and</I> Fiero mechanic!) my services are available to you anytime you may need them......You have done a remarkable job on your site and belive me, it is due to your efforts that the Fiero community is growing as it is on here.<P>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 01-14-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 01-14-2001).]||||reg||1
